config BR2_PACKAGE_CHERRY
	bool "cherry"
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_OPENCHAMBER
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_SYSTEMD_MACHINED # the user's containers
	depends on BR2_PACKAGE_SYSTEMD_POLKIT # its machinectl privileges
	help
	  Cherry's own service: the cherry user, with /var/lib/cherry as
	  its home, and cherry.service, which runs OpenChamber's server
	  as that user, listening on 127.0.0.1:3000. Given the systemd
	  credential openchamber.ui_password, it listens on every
	  address instead, with that password on the browser UI.
	  cherry-connect-url.service shows the link that pairs another
	  OpenChamber app with it on the console, once it is online.

	  The cherry user manages containers: polkit rules let it start,
	  stop, enter and remove them with machinectl, and start
	  cherry-bootstrap@.service, which creates one as root with
	  debootstrap, rpmstrap or pacstrap.
